  "correction_rules": [
    "Persistent positive bias: forecasts are systematically too high versus realized prices (often by ~5–15 EUR) across the full 30d horizon; apply a downward level shift to the entire path.",
    "Missed regime shift / mean-reversion failure: when history shows a topping pattern and initial drawdown, the model continues to project mid/high-70s to mid-80s instead of following the downtrend; add a rule to detect post-peak breakdowns and force a lower trend channel.",
    "Horizon-dependent overshoot: error tends to grow with horizon (later days often most overestimated); increase downward correction with lead time (e.g., small cut days 1–5, larger cut days 15–30).",
    "Insufficient downside momentum: the model underestimates the speed and depth of declines (realized drops are sharper); increase negative drift when recent returns are negative and volatility is elevated.",
    "Overreaction to prior highs: forecasts anchor to recent highs (80–84) even after prices fall into low-70s/high-60s; cap forecasts relative to recent rolling mean/median (e.g., limit to mean + k·vol) and enforce faster mean reversion downward after peaks."
  ]
